# What stays out of the .vsix.
#
# Everything the host needs is bundled into
# dist/extension.cjs, so neither the source nor the
# dependency tree ships.
#
# One rule to be careful with: dist/ also carries
# assets the extension copies into a new project,
# including TypeScript templates read from core.
# A pattern aimed at source by file type — **/*.ts
# and the like — would sweep those up, and the
# package would install, activate, and then fail at
# the one moment it was asked to make a project.
# Exclude by directory, not by extension.

.claude/**
.github/**
.vscode/**
src/**
test/**
tests/**
test-results/**
playwright-report/**
mboss-core/**
mboss-mcp-server/**
mboss-skills/**
node_modules/**

# Written for whoever works on this extension, the
# way the skills under .claude/ are, and not for
# whoever installs it. README.md and
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md are the two that ship.
CLAUDE.md

.gitignore
.gitmodules
.nvmrc
.prettierignore
.prettierrc.json
eslint.config.mjs
package-lock.json
playwright.config.ts
tsconfig.json
vitest.aliases.ts
vitest.config.ts
vitest.integration.config.ts

*.tsbuildinfo
*.vsix
